            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lilcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a mellow comforting kind of soup. True to the simple to make claim, it took 15 minutes to prep and 15 to cook as I cut up the potatoes in very small pieces. I used 2 cups half and half and 1 cup skim as I have half and half to use up. Regarding the milk, I can see it would be just as good as written. I served it with Jim's Cheese Soda Bread from this site. I will make this again!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "normal"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I omitted the bacon and the bell pepper because I didn’t have any. Also I used imitation crab meat. Use imitation crab meat often verses the real thing. I used some fish stock and cayenne pepper besides the other seasonings listed in the recipe. This was enjoyed by all and I am saving this recipe for future use.",
            "datePublished": "2024-03-28T00:03:55.308Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "stobiasz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very bland. Added some Old Bay after serving and it made it edible, but not what I was going for.",
            "datePublished": "2019-09-28T14:15:16.227Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brooklyn Krehmeyer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really enjoyed this soup with some substations! I added 6 medium sized potatoes diced, I caramelized the onions and added 3 portobello mushrooms with agave syrup. I added basil, onion powder, oregano, bay seasoning, and garlic salt to the soup. Roughly a teaspoon of each. I did not use skim milk but just regular whole milk and instead of half and half I used heavy whipping cream. Next time, I’ll add a can of corn. It sorta tasted like a clam chowder base soup and I really enjoyed it!",
            "datePublished": "2019-04-12T01:43:23.157Z"
          },
